alms:
My soul is not a pauper; I can live
At least my soul’s life, without alms from men;
And if it must be in heaven instead of earth,

almighty:
A hissing and a butt for pointing hands,
Whilst God Almighty hunts and grinds us thus;
For He hath scattered us in alien lands,

almanacs:
Told you when the day was near,
Did n't need no almanacs;
That was one o' Nature's fac's.

almos:
Moufs mus' be a-wat'rin' roun' hyeah fuh a mile;
Den we almos' hollah ez we hu'ies down,
'Ca'se hit's apple dumplin's, big an' fat an' brown!
